make_asset(): count each child once (upstream issue #8).

`make_asset` fills `sons` twice — once in the loop that sums bone lengths
and again in the loop that jitters coincident joints — so every joint
carries each child twice. `len(sons[i]) == 1` is then never true: the
`connect_tail_to_unique_child` branch never runs, and `extrude_from_parent`
fires for every bone instead. The tails come out as a fixed stub along the
parent direction rather than reaching the child, which is what an exported
armature is judged on and what a viewer draws.

One line: drop the second append. The jitter loop needs `p` and the
distance, not the child list.

See designs/hosting.md, "SkinTokens", and
https://github.com/VAST-AI-Research/SkinTokens/issues/8. Against
VAST-AI-Research/SkinTokens @ 273b691d.

